WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.760
Another list of grants, but which ones fit?

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:06.680
Here is how Sharke helps you review an opportunity and decide

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:08.520
what to check next.

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:11.640
Let's look at Riverbend, a fictional nonprofit.

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:15.780
It needs funding for after-school tutoring and summer reading programs.

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:19.140
First, we work out how much those programs need and subtract

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:21.140
the funding already committed.

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:23.860
We don't count pending applications as money you have.

00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:28.780
Sharke organizes the grants you're considering into a funding pipeline.

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:31.900
You can see the deadlines, then review why each grant might

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:33.380
fit your program.

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:36.700
Here, the app shows a strong match for Riverbend's work and

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:37.760
location.

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:41.360
It also shows that the funder's history has not been verified.

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:43.220
That still needs checking.

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:46.000
When you're ready to apply, you have a first draft based

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:48.180
on your materials and the funder's requirements.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:52.320
Check the details about your program and its results, review the

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:55.340
draft, and submit the application yourself.

00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:58.620
Keep the system you already use to manage your contacts.

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:02.240
You can export your grant list, deadlines and decisions to share

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:04.140
with your team or board.

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:07.680
I've worked as a strategy consultant for Fortune 500 and FTSE

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:11.560
100 companies, and as a technology executive and an investor.

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:15.720
Across those roles, I helped businesses decide where to put their

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:17.260
time and money.

00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:20.520
I've also done the grant work firsthand, winning more than one

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:24.120
million dollars in federal funding across several awards.

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:27.860
I founded Sharke to help nonprofits build a pipeline capable of

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:29.420
funding their mission.

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:32.460
We work out how big that pipeline needs to be, find

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:36.080
the right funding opportunities, and support the work needed to pursue

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:36.980
and win them.

00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:41.040
Grant Team starts at ninety-nine dollars a month for organizations with

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:43.740
annual revenue under one million dollars.

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:47.420
Your price depends on your organization's annual revenue.

00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:50.860
Plans are month to month, and you can cancel anytime.

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:54.380
After you sign up, check your organization's profile and add the

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:56.780
materials needed for your applications.

00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:59.900
Then review the grants in your pipeline and the evidence behind

00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:01.020
each one.

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:04.060
Visit Sharke dot A I slash grant director to choose your

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:04.380
plan.

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:08.440
Confirm your profile to get started building your funding pipeline, with

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:10.280
application support to move it forward.
